    <string name="pc_setup_instructions"> <b>Step 1: Run MYRA Companion on your PC</b>"
 You need Node.js installed (nodejs.org), then run node companion.js from the MYRA Companion folder. It prints your PC's IP address and a 6-digit PIN in the terminal - that PIN is what you enter below, nowhere else generates or checks it.

 "<b>Step 2: Allow it through the Firewall</b>"
 Windows usually prompts you to allow it the first time - choose Private networks. If you don't see a prompt, open it manually:
 1. Press the Windows key and type Windows Defender Firewall with Advanced Security.
 2. Click "<b>Inbound Rules</b> (on the left), then <b>New Rule...</b>" (on the right).
 3. Select "<b>Port</b>" and click Next.
 4. Select "<b>TCP</b> and type <b>8080</b>" in Specific local ports.
 5. Select "<b>Allow the connection</b>" and click Next.
 6. Keep all boxes checked (Domain, Private, Public) and click Next.
 7. Name it MYRA Companion and click Finish.

 "<b>Step 3: Connect</b>"
 Make sure your PC and phone are on the same Wi-Fi, then enter the IP address and PIN from the Companion's terminal window above and tap Connect. "</string>
